# Chapter: Basics - TCP stdio bridge (nc-lite)
# Shows: net.tcp_connect/net.tcp_listen/net.tcp_accept socket objects
#        (TcpConn send/recv/close, TcpListener accept) behind `lmdebug pipe`
# Run: lmscript examples/pipe.lms      (then: lmdebug --lmcode build/pipe.dslb)
# Needs: nothing (offline); a live socket roundtrip needs a peer process,
#        so this script only probes port 1 (closed on practically every
#        machine — the verdict is data, not an error, so no assertion pins
#        it) and prints how to drive the CLI bridge. A refused
#        net.tcp_connect throws dslvm::Error and lmscript has no recover,
#        so no connect attempt is made here.
# exit: 0
# expect:
#|pipe example
#|bridge: lmdebug pipe HOST PORT  (or lmdebug pipe --listen PORT [--forever])
p = _dsl_ cli="lmdebug" install="github:lmctl-ai/lmdebug@latest";

println("pipe example");
println("bridge: lmdebug pipe HOST PORT  (or lmdebug pipe --listen PORT [--forever])");
println("port 1 reachable: " + str(net.check("127.0.0.1", 1)));
println("objects: net.tcp_connect -> TcpConn{send,recv,close}; net.tcp_listen -> TcpListener{accept}");

end _dsl_
savedsl(p, "build/pipe.dslb");
